(1. Purpose) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This process describes how the Platform Engineering team releases changes to production) Tj
T*
(services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Applies to all application deployments to the production environment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Release Authorisation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Production releases require authorisation by a release manager who did not implement) Tj
T*
(the change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 The release manager records their approval in the deployment ticket before the) Tj
T*
(release pipeline is triggered.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Pre-Release Verification) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 All changes are deployed to the staging environment and verified by the implementing) Tj
T*
(engineer before a production release is scheduled.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 The engineer confirms that a rollback approach exists before deploying. Rollback) Tj
T*
(steps are discussed during the release call.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Emergency Releases) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 Emergency releases may be deployed immediately at the discretion of the on-call) Tj
T*
(engineer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
